We are given that Skyler has 100 hats in total.
Half of the hats are red, so $R = \frac{1}{2} \times 100 = 50$.
The remaining hats are $100 - R = 100 - 50 = 50$.
3/5 of the remaining hats are blue, so $B = \frac{3}{5} \times 50 = 3 \times 10 = 30$.
The rest are white. The number of white hats is the total number of hats minus the number of red hats and the number of blue hats.
So, $W = 100 - R - B = 100 - 50 - 30 = 100 - 80 = 20$.
The number of white hats is 20.

